-- §4b  Every question the absence census actually files a row under.
# One row per distinct question in epistemics/absences.sqlc. This is the other side of §4: a
# question the census files under and the roster does not name is an arm nobody declared, and its
# rows count toward no column. The program takes the difference in Rust, against §4's roster.
#
# What it cannot see
#   Only questions that filed something appear, because a relation derived from rows cannot list an
#   arm that produced none. §4 covers that half from the roster's side.
-- epistemics/absences.sqlc, its questions.
SELECT DISTINCT a.question AS "question!"
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/absences.sqlc)
) a
ORDER BY a.question
